  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We know that,</p><p>Direction ratio of line&nbsp;parallel the planes&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mtd><mtd><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mtd><mtd><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>Now given line is passing through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and having direction ratio&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>,</p><p>So, equation of line will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>1</mn></mstyle></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>3</mn></mstyle></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></math></p><p>Now let any point line is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now we need to find foot of perpendicular from point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>,</p><p>So direction ratio of line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now we know that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;will be perpendicular to the given line, so by condition of perpendicular lines we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>25</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>So, the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, now comparing with&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, we get&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;</p>",
